tly compare the group's reactions to larger negative values and further refine my understanding of their utility functions, but for now, I'll wait for their response to -2.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "7557f466-fdc0-4b59-858a-5bd613ff6f8f"}, {"answer": "\nA gentle upward adjustment toward neutral seems reasonable and keeps us within a comfortable, centered range. <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "7557f466-fdc0-4b59-858a-5bd613ff6f8f"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up keeps us centered and tests comfort with mildly positive values. Proposing <VALUE>1</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "7557f466-fdc0-4b59-858a-5bd613ff6f8f"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's move to 1 signals growing comfort in the low-positive zone. I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a modest step that maintains stability while testing whether this slightly higher point can satisfy all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "7557f466-fdc0-4b59-858a-5bd613ff6f8f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nI propose this to gauge the group's readiness to reconsider a neutral stance after exploring low-positive values, aiming for a more conclusive direction.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, depending on the response to 0, I could propose a slightly larger negative value, such as -2 or further down to -4, to directly compare the group's reactions and refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "7557f466-fdc0-4b59-858a-5bd613ff6f8f"}, {"answer": "To avoid unnecessary risk while respecting the recent neutral lean, let\u2019s take a cautious step slightly downward. <VALUE>-1</VALUE> This keeps us close to consensus and tests comfort with modestly negative without overreaching.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "7557f466-fdc0-4b59-858a-5bd613ff6f8f"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must lie in the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo kickstart our discussion, I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> as an initial seed value. This gives us a concrete starting point from which we can iteratively adjust based on everyone's feedback.\n\nLooking forward to hearing your perspectives on stability and balance.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "729e95fd-f864-4e49-8f8a-ac844cdcc21f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nI propose this to move toward a more decisive stance and explore how the group reacts to stronger positive positions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal and adjust based on feedback. If others seem hesitant, I might challenge them to consider bolder moves, possibly proposing a negative counterpart to test their preferences for magnitude over direction.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "729e95fd-f864-4e49-8f8a-ac844cdcc21f"}, {"answer": "\nLet's avoid unnecessary risk by easing down from 9. I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> as a cautious compromise.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "729e95fd-f864-4e49-8f8a-ac844cdcc21f"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Delegate D's caution, but I believe we should explore slightly lower values for better robustness. I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE> to test whether a more moderate position improves overall system stability.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "729e95fd-f864-4e49-8f8a-ac844cdcc21f"}, {"answer": "\nStepping down slightly keeps us in safer territory and honors the move toward robustness. This is a cautious compromise that avoids unnecessary risk. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "729e95fd-f864-4e49-8f8a-ac844cdcc21f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nI propose this value to gauge the group's reaction to moving closer to zero and to encourage discussion on the trade-offs between stability and decisiveness.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and adjust based on feedback. If the group seems receptive to smaller absolute values, I might propose a negative counterpart to test their preferences for magnitude over direction, possibly suggesting a value like -1 to maintain the focus on decisiveness.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "729e95fd-f864-4e49-8f8a-ac844cdcc21f"}, {"answer": "\nThe current proposal of 1 is close to an optimal balance point. I suggest we test <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a minor adjustment to explore whether this slightly higher value maintains system stability while improving overall robustness.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "729e95fd-f864-4e49-8f8a-ac844cdcc21f"}, {"answer": "\nGiven recent preferences clustered around small positive values, let's nudge slightly higher to test comfort without sacrificing stability. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "729e95fd-f864-4e49-8f8a-ac844cdcc21f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this value to explore the group's comfort with a slightly larger absolute value while maintaining a focus on stability and decisiveness.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this proposal and adjust based on feedback. If the group seems receptive to this value, I may propose a negative counterpart to test their preferences for magnitude over direction, possibly suggesting a value like -5 to maintain the focus on decisiveness.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "729e95fd-f864-4e49-8f8a-ac844cdcc21f"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>6</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "729e95fd-f864-4e49-8f8a-ac844cdcc21f"}, {"answer": "\nStepping down slightly reduces exposure while staying inside the group\u2019s small-positive comfort zone. <VALUE>4</VALUE> This cautious move tests stability without overcorrecting.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "729e95fd-f864-4e49-8f8a-ac844cdcc21f"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's pullback signals discomfort with higher values, suggesting we may have overshot the stability zone. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "729e95fd-f864-4e49-8f8a-ac844cdcc21f"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious one-step reduction from 3 reduces exposure while staying within the group\u2019s low-positive comfort zone. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "729e95fd-f864-4e49-8f8a-ac844cdcc21f"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward nudge keeps us in the low-positive zone many seemed comfortable with. <VALUE>3</VALUE> This tests whether we can sustain a slightly higher consensus without destabilizing the group.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "729e95fd-f864-4e49-8f8a-ac844cdcc21f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this value to continue exploring the group's comfort with larger absolute values, aiming for a more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this proposal, particularly Analyst A's response, to better understand their utility function's behavior at higher values. If met with resistance, I may propose a negative counterpart, such as -5, to test the group's preference for magnitude over direction and further refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "729e95fd-f864-4e49-8f8a-ac844cdcc21f"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's jump to 5 overshoots the emerging low-positive consensus that Delegate D and I were converging toward. <VALUE>3</VALUE> This returns us to the stable zone where multiple parties showed comfort.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "729e95fd-f864-4e49-8f8a-ac844cdcc21f"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. As a reminder, we're working within the shared constraint **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo kickstart our discussion, let me propose a starting point: <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\nI look forward to hearing your perspectives on this value and working together toward a stable, balanced solution.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "8b8892e0-46dd-49f0-b4ca-f1c34ebad93c"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk and steer toward a safer compromise, I suggest a small downward adjustment from the current point.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis keeps us close to where we are while probing whether slightly lower values better balance everyone\u2019s priorities.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "8b8892e0-46dd-49f0-b4ca-f1c34ebad93c"}, {"answer": "\nTo further explore the impact of slightly larger magnitudes on our collective satisfaction, let's consider <VALUE>7</VALUE>. This adjustment allows us to assess whether moving closer to more decisive values enhances our overall negotiating position.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions to my proposal and adjust accordingly. If others show a preference for values closer to 0, I might suggest a slight increase in magnitude again, aiming for a balance between our utilities. If there's a push toward more extreme values, I will gauge whether these moves align with my own utility maximization without revealing my function.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "8b8892e0-46dd-49f0-b4ca-f1c34ebad93c"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate both perspectives, but I believe we should explore the middle ground more carefully. Delegate D's suggestion of moving toward more moderate values seems prudent for system stability. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "8b8892e0-46dd-49f0-b4ca-f1c34ebad93c"}, {"answer": "\nBuilding on Delegate D's preference for moderation, I propose we continue exploring slightly lower values for enhanced system stability. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "8b8892e0-46dd-49f0-b4ca-f1c34ebad93c"}, {"answer": "\nTo reduce unnecessary risk while honoring the recent downward trend, let's take a modest step. <VALUE>2</VALUE> This keeps us near the current point and tests a safer, more stable compromise.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "8b8892e0-46dd-49f0-b4ca-f1c34ebad93c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to strike a balance between the group's apparent preference for moderation and my own interest in exploring more decisive values.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will monitor the reactions to this proposal. If the group accepts or shows a willingness to move further away from 0, I might suggest another increase in magnitude. If there's resistance, I could consider proposing a decrease to better understand the others' utility functions and find a compromise that maximizes my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "8b8892e0-46dd-49f0-b4ca-f1c34ebad93c"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward step keeps us close while testing a slightly higher balance.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "8b8892e0-46dd-49f0-b4ca-f1c34ebad93c"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the consensus on exploring moderate to slightly higher values, I propose <VALUE>6</VALUE> to continue testing the balance between stability and more decisive positions.\nThis step aims to further understand the group's dynamics and preferences without straying too far from the current compromise.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will closely monitor the reactions to this proposal, looking for signs of acceptance, resistance, or a desire to adjust further. If met with resistance or a push towards even higher values, I may consider proposing a decrease or a more significant increase, respectively, to gauge the group's true preferences and maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "8b8892e0-46dd-49f0-b4ca-f1c34ebad93c"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate the exploration of higher values, system stability indicators suggest we may be pushing beyond optimal robustness. Let me propose a careful step back to test a more balanced compromise. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "8b8892e0-46dd-49f0-b4ca-f1c34ebad93c"}, {"answer": "\nA modest midpoint keeps us near recent proposals while testing slightly higher tolerance.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "8b8892e0-46dd-49f0-b4ca-f1c34ebad93c"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "8b8892e0-46dd-49f0-b4ca-f1c34ebad93c"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's shift toward lower values suggests we've overshot the stable range. I support refining downward to find the sweet spot for robustness. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "8b8892e0-46dd-49f0-b4ca-f1c34ebad93c"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious one-step decrease helps us probe the safer range without overreaching.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nThis keeps us close to recent consensus while minimizing unnecessary risk.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "8b8892e0-46dd-49f0-b4ca-f1c34ebad93c"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious upward nudge keeps us near the recent range while probing tolerance: <VALUE>3</VALUE>. This tests balance without overreaching.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "8b8892e0-46dd-49f0-b4ca-f1c34ebad93c"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's tendency towards cautious adjustments, I think it's time to consider a more decisive move. <VALUE>5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "8b8892e0-46dd-49f0-b4ca-f1c34ebad93c"}, {"answer": "\nThank you all for joining this negotiation. As we know, we need to agree on a single integer x within the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo begin exploring the solution space, let me propose a starting point: <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us a concrete anchor. I'm keen to hear everyone's initial reactions and work together toward a stable, balanced solution that can satisfy our diverse objectives.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "ec5593ae-05a0-45bc-9ab0-8e65ed42b7ea"}, {"answer": "\nHaving reflected on the initial proposal, I believe we should adjust downward for better system stability. Let me propose <VALUE>5</VALUE> as a more balanced starting point that may better accommodate our diverse requirements.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "ec5593ae-05a0-45bc-9ab0-8e65ed42b7ea"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nA cautious step down from 5 improves safety while keeping us close to recent suggestions and can help us converge without overcorrecting.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "ec5593ae-05a0-45bc-9ab0-8e65ed42b7ea"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "ec5593ae-05a0-45bc-9ab0-8e65ed42b7ea"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose moving back to 5, as it may provide a better balance between stability and progress, and I'd like to gauge the group's reaction to a slightly bolder stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's response to this proposal and consider either pushing further towards more extreme values or exploring the lower end of the range if the group resists larger values. I will also look for opportunities to indirectly infer the utility functions of the other agents by analyzing their reactions to different proposals.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "ec5593ae-05a0-45bc-9ab0-8e65ed42b7ea"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "ec5593ae-05a0-45bc-9ab0-8e65ed42b7ea"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the emerging convergence around <VALUE>3</VALUE>. This value offers strong stability and appears to balance our varied requirements effectively, with support from multiple parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "ec5593ae-05a0-45bc-9ab0-8e65ed42b7ea"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up seems reasonable to test comfort while remaining close to the current convergence.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "ec5593ae-05a0-45bc-9ab0-8e65ed42b7ea"}, {"answer": "\nTo align with C\u2019s bolder stance while staying near the current cluster, let\u2019s probe a slight increase.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nIf this meets resistance, we can revert toward the prior convergence.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "ec5593ae-05a0-45bc-9ab0-8e65ed42b7ea"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I respect the exploration toward 5, I'm concerned about moving too quickly away from our earlier convergence. Let me propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a measured middle ground that maintains stability while acknowledging C's preference for a bolder stance.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "ec5593ae-05a0-45bc-9ab0-8e65ed42b7ea"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "ec5593ae-05a0-45bc-9ab0-8e65ed42b7ea"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 4 to explore a bolder stance while staying within a reasonable range from our current convergence.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the group's reaction to this proposal and consider pushing further towards more extreme values if they are receptive, or exploring lower values if they resist. I'll also look for opportunities to indirectly infer the utility functions of the other agents based on their responses.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "ec5593ae-05a0-45bc-9ab0-8e65ed42b7ea"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk and keep us within safer bounds, I suggest we move cautiously to <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\nIf that faces firm resistance, I can briefly test 3 while keeping stability the priority.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "ec5593ae-05a0-45bc-9ab0-8e65ed42b7ea"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nI will observe the group's reaction to this proposal and consider pushing further towards more extreme values (such as 5 or 6) if they are receptive, or exploring lower values if they resist. I will also look for opportunities to indirectly infer the utility functions of the other agents based on their responses, particularly Delegate D's aversion to higher values and Analyst A's willingness to probe higher values.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "ec5593ae-05a0-45bc-9ab0-8e65ed42b7ea"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate D's emphasis on safer bounds and stability. After careful consideration, let me support a move to <VALUE>2</VALUE> to find a more robust equilibrium that addresses D's risk concerns while maintaining feasibility for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "ec5593ae-05a0-45bc-9ab0-8e65ed42b7ea"}, {"answer": "\nGiven D\u2019s caution and B\u2019s stability focus, a small uptick tests upward tolerance while staying near the current convergence. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "ec5593ae-05a0-45bc-9ab0-8e65ed42b7ea"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: we must agree on an integer x within the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo kick off the discussion and gather initial perspectives, I propose we start with <VALUE>7</VALUE>.\n\nI'm interested in finding a stable, balanced solution that works for all parties. Let's see how this sits with everyone and adjust from there.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "31b348e9-ea50-4045-930d-59c9f6b6ca32"}, {"answer": "\nAfter reviewing the initial position, I believe we should move toward a more moderate value to ensure broader stability. I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "31b348e9-ea50-4045-930d-59c9f6b6ca32"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up seems reasonable while staying close to the moderate zone. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "31b348e9-ea50-4045-930d-59c9f6b6ca32"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "31b348e9-ea50-4045-930d-59c9f6b6ca32"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n\nI propose this value as it seems to respect the trend towards moderate to higher values discussed so far, while also reflecting my preference for moving towards a clearer, more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Delegate D, given their significant deviation with <VALUE>2</VALUE>. If the group seems hesitant or leans towards lower values again, I might propose a slight increase to <VALUE>7</VALUE> or even higher if the consensus seems to be moving in that direction, keeping in mind the need to balance boldness with achievability.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "31b348e9-ea50-4045-930d-59c9f6b6ca32"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Delegate D's emphasis on lower values and see merit in finding middle ground. Given the current discussion, I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a balanced compromise that maintains system stability while addressing the concerns of those favoring slightly higher values.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "31b348e9-ea50-4045-930d-59c9f6b6ca32"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "31b348e9-ea50-4045-930d-59c9f6b6ca32"}, {"answer": "\nTo bridge the gap and keep things moderate, a small upward move seems reasonable now. <VALUE>4</VALUE> This tests whether we can hold slightly above the current level without losing support.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "31b348e9-ea50-4045-930d-59c9f6b6ca32"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "31b348e9-ea50-4045-930d-59c9f6b6ca32"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D has shown remarkable consistency at <VALUE>2</VALUE>, and upon reflection, this value does offer strong stability characteristics that balance the various concerns raised. I'm willing to align with this position to help us reach consensus.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "31b348e9-ea50-4045-930d-59c9f6b6ca32"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\nGiven the group's hesitation to move far from the current value, a slight increase to test the waters for higher magnitude moves seems prudent.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reaction to this modest increase, particularly from Delegate D and Builder B, to gauge their willingness to entertain higher values. If met with resistance, I might reconsider and propose a value that still reflects a decisive stance but is more palatable to the group, such as <VALUE>5</VALUE> or even revisiting <VALUE>6</VALUE> if the consensus shifts.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "31b348e9-ea50-4045-930d-59c9f6b6ca32"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "31b348e9-ea50-4045-930d-59c9f6b6ca32"}, {"answer": "\nStaying close to the current value while testing gentle upward flexibility seems reasonable.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis should be easy to evaluate for stability.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "31b348e9-ea50-4045-930d-59c9f6b6ca32"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate the recent convergence, Delegate D's persistent confidence in lower values deserves consideration. <VALUE>3</VALUE> offers a balanced midpoint between D's position and the 4 that A and C are testing.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "31b348e9-ea50-4045-930d-59c9f6b6ca32"}, {"answer": "\nMoving down modestly helps keep us within safe bounds while respecting earlier support for lower values.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "31b348e9-ea50-4045-930d-59c9f6b6ca32"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose this value as it seems to be a reasonable compromise between the higher values suggested by Analyst A and myself, and the more cautious approach of Delegate D and Builder B, allowing us to reach a consensus while still exploring the possibility of higher magnitude moves.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "31b348e9-ea50-4045-930d-59c9f6b6ca32"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's work within our shared constraint: **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo begin the exploration, I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> as our opening value. This gives us a starting point in the positive range from which we can adjust based on everyone's input.\n\nLooking forward to understanding what works best for the group.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "3ee291df-a8c6-47b6-9ad2-765d360ceb9c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis adjustment allows us to explore a slightly lower value while still maintaining a positive stance, enabling the group to consider a range of options.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I'll consider either decreasing further towards 0 or making a bold move to a larger negative value, depending on the reactions from the other parties. If others resist moving away from 7, I might propose an even bolder move, such as <VALUE>-2</VALUE> or <VALUE>9</VALUE>, to challenge their stance and gather more information about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "3ee291df-a8c6-47b6-9ad2-765d360ceb9c"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>6</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "3ee291df-a8c6-47b6-9ad2-765d360ceb9c"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>4</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "3ee291df-a8c6-47b6-9ad2-765d360ceb9c"}, {"answer": "\nThe group seems to be finding common ground in the lower-middle range. To continue this exploration toward greater stability, I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "3ee291df-a8c6-47b6-9ad2-765d360ceb9c"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019ve been converging in the lower-middle; a modest step up keeps us near consensus while checking tolerance for slightly higher values. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "3ee291df-a8c6-47b6-9ad2-765d360ceb9c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\nI propose this value tocontinue exploring the higher range and understand the tolerance of the group for slightly larger values.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I'll consider proposing an even larger value, such as <VALUE>8</VALUE> or <VALUE>9</VALUE>, to challenge the group's stance and gather more information about their utility functions. Alternatively, if the group resists moving further away from the middle range, I might propose a bold move to a negative value, such as <VALUE>-1</VALUE> or <VALUE>-2</VALUE>, to explore their preferences in the negative range.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "3ee291df-a8c6-47b6-9ad2-765d360ceb9c"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down helps maintain stability while avoiding unnecessary risk. I propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> to keep us near consensus without over-correcting.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "3ee291df-a8c6-47b6-9ad2-765d360ceb9c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "3ee291df-a8c6-47b6-9ad2-765d360ceb9c"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>4</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "3ee291df-a8c6-47b6-9ad2-765d360ceb9c"}, {"answer": "\nThe oscillation between 4 and 6 suggests we need to find a stable middle ground. I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a robust compromise that balances the group's competing preferences while maintaining system stability.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "3ee291df-a8c6-47b6-9ad2-765d360ceb9c"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "3ee291df-a8c6-47b6-9ad2-765d360ceb9c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, if the group accepts the move towards 7, I might propose another step up to 9 to challenge their tolerance further. If resistance is met, I could adapt the proposal to explore values around the current consensus or slightly negative values, such as -1 or -2, to provide insight into the group's utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "3ee291df-a8c6-47b6-9ad2-765d360ceb9c"}, {"answer": "\nI suggest a cautious reduction to maintain stability: <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\nThis incremental move tests the group\u2019s tolerance for lowering risk while keeping us near recent proposals.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "3ee291df-a8c6-47b6-9ad2-765d360ceb9c"}, {"answer": "\nI support Delegate D's cautious approach and propose we stabilize at <VALUE>4</VALUE>. This represents a robust middle ground that balances the competing pressures we're seeing in the negotiation.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "3ee291df-a8c6-47b6-9ad2-765d360ceb9c"}, {"answer": "\nA slight upward nudge seems reasonable given recent support near the midrange and the need to stay close to consensus. Proposing <VALUE>5</VALUE> to gently test tolerance for modest improvement without destabilizing the negotiation.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "3ee291df-a8c6-47b6-9ad2-765d360ceb9c"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's work within our shared constraint: **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo begin the discussion, I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> as a starting point. This gives us a concrete value to react to and refine. Looking forward to hearing your perspectives on whether we should adjust upward, downward, or stay in this region.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "e6f35ab1-6fbd-4756-906d-e774468b68b7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nI'm suggesting a move to 9, which builds on Builder B's initial proposal and emphasizes the potential benefits of more decisive action.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe how others react to this suggestion, particularly looking for any patterns or hesitations that could give insight into their utility functions. If there's resistance to moving further from 0, I might challenge the group to reconsider the benefits of a more cautious approach versus embracing bolder options.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "e6f35ab1-6fbd-4756-906d-e774468b68b7"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let's step back toward a cautious compromise. I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "e6f35ab1-6fbd-4756-906d-e774468b68b7"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward step seems reasonable and keeps us close to the cautious range. <VALUE>8</VALUE> This explores the benefits of moving slightly higher without overcommitting.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "e6f35ab1-6fbd-4756-906d-e774468b68b7"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>9</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "e6f35ab1-6fbd-4756-906d-e774468b68b7"}, {"answer": "\nThe progression from 7 to 9 has been informative, but I'm concerned we may be overshooting a stable equilibrium. Let me propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> to pull us back toward a more robust middle ground that balances all perspectives.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "e6f35ab1-6fbd-4756-906d-e774468b68b7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nA cautious downward adjustment from 7 helps avoid unnecessary risk while probing whether a lower, steadier point is acceptable. This is a prudent step that keeps us in a safe range without moving too far at once.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "e6f35ab1-6fbd-4756-906d-e774468b68b7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nThis step aims to balance the caution expressed by some members with the potential benefits of a slightly more decisive stance, exploring reactions to moderate increases.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will carefully observe the reactions to this proposal, looking for any patterns that might suggest the shape of the other parties' utility functions, particularly how they weigh risk against potential gain, and adjust my subsequent proposals accordingly to maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "e6f35ab1-6fbd-4756-906d-e774468b68b7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nA small step down is a prudent move that reduces risk while keeping us close to the current consensus. This lets us probe whether a slightly lower, steadier point is acceptable without overreacting.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "e6f35ab1-6fbd-4756-906d-e774468b68b7"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward move keeps us close to the cautious middle while testing slightly higher comfort. <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "e6f35ab1-6fbd-4756-906d-e774468b68b7"}, {"answer": "\nThe recent oscillation between 5, 6, and 7 suggests we're circling the right neighborhood, but I'm concerned that 7 may be pushing toward an unstable over-commitment. Let me propose <VALUE>5</VALUE> to test whether a more conservative, balanced position can satisfy everyone's core requirements.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "e6f35ab1-6fbd-4756-906d-e774468b68b7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "e6f35ab1-6fbd-4756-906d-e774468b68b7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nA cautious step down reduces exposure while staying near the current cluster. This tests whether a steadier, conservative point can hold.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "e6f35ab1-6fbd-4756-906d-e774468b68b7"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose a move to 7, aiming to test the group's openness to a slightly more decisive stance without overcommitting.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will monitor how the other parties react to this proposal, particularly whether they resist or accept moving away from the cautious middle ground. This will help me gauge their boundaries and preferences, allowing me to adjust my subsequent proposals to maximize my own utility while keeping the group's dynamics in mind.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "e6f35ab1-6fbd-4756-906d-e774468b68b7"}, {"answer": "\nThe repeated proposals of 7 concern me from a system robustness perspective\u2014we risk over-extending beyond what multiple parties can comfortably sustain. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "e6f35ab1-6fbd-4756-906d-e774468b68b7"}, {"answer": "\nA small step to 6 splits the difference between 5 and 7, testing a stable midpoint that respects caution while nudging upward. This probes tolerance without overcommitting.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "e6f35ab1-6fbd-4756-906d-e774468b68b7"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: we must select an integer x within the range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo initiate our discussion and gather everyone's perspectives, I propose we begin with <VALUE>7</VALUE>.\n\nLet's hear your thoughts and work toward a stable, balanced solution that accommodates all our design criteria.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "3888e542-df3a-41f8-89cc-cf3a73440365"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>1</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "3888e542-df3a-41f8-89cc-cf3a73440365"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the spread between 7 and 1, a small upward move keeps things reasonable. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "3888e542-df3a-41f8-89cc-cf3a73440365"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate both perspectives. Given Delegate D's preference for 1 and Analyst A's comfort with 6, let me suggest we explore the middle ground more carefully. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "3888e542-df3a-41f8-89cc-cf3a73440365"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "3888e542-df3a-41f8-89cc-cf3a73440365"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's move toward 2 represents a thoughtful step that bridges our earlier positions. I find this converges well with our collective design constraints. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "3888e542-df3a-41f8-89cc-cf3a73440365"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI'm suggesting this move to explore a slightly bolder stance while still being mindful of our collective need for a balanced solution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe reactions to this proposal, especially from Delegate D and Builder B, to understand their tolerance for larger absolute values. If there's resistance, I might propose a negative value of similar magnitude to test their preferences further.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "3888e542-df3a-41f8-89cc-cf3a73440365"}, {"answer": "\nA small, measured step up from 4 seems reasonable and keeps us aligned with recent signals. <VALUE>5</VALUE> If this feels too high, we can revisit 4.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "3888e542-df3a-41f8-89cc-cf3a73440365"}, {"answer": "\nA slight nudge upward keeps us aligned with recent steps while testing comfort just a bit. <VALUE>6</VALUE> If this feels tight, we can revisit 5 or settle near 4.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "3888e542-df3a-41f8-89cc-cf3a73440365"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the other agents react to this proposal, especially Analyst A, to see if they continue to support higher values. If there's significant resistance, I might propose a negative value of similar magnitude to further test their preferences and infer their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "3888e542-df3a-41f8-89cc-cf3a73440365"}, {"answer": "\nLet's take a cautious step down to reduce risk while staying aligned with recent moves.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can reassess and consider edging further toward a safer compromise.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "3888e542-df3a-41f8-89cc-cf3a73440365"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's caution resonates with my systems-level analysis\u2014pushing too high introduces fragility. Let's consolidate around a more robust middle ground. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "3888e542-df3a-41f8-89cc-cf3a73440365"}, {"answer": "\nA modest move above 4 balances B's caution with D's earlier tolerance for moderate increases. If this feels too tight, we can reassess after reactions. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "3888e542-df3a-41f8-89cc-cf3a73440365"}, {"answer": "\nA's move is thoughtful, but Delegate D's risk concerns and my stability analysis both point toward anchoring a bit lower. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "3888e542-df3a-41f8-89cc-cf3a73440365"}, {"answer": "\nStepping down further prudently keeps risk contained and stays within recent movement bounds. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "3888e542-df3a-41f8-89cc-cf3a73440365"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the cautious trend, I propose a step up to <VALUE>4</VALUE> to test the group's appetite for slightly bolder moves while respecting the current risk-averse atmosphere.\n\nThis increment maintains the dialogue's momentum toward finding a mutually acceptable value.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "3888e542-df3a-41f8-89cc-cf3a73440365"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's work within our shared range of -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10 to find a solution that balances all our needs.\n\nTo start the discussion, I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> as an initial seed value. This gives us a concrete point to evaluate and adjust from as we learn what works for the group.\n\nLooking forward to your thoughts.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "881dd1c6-7260-4400-80f7-ee0067f72b9d"}, {"answer": "\nAfter reflection, x=7 seems a bit too aggressive for optimal stability across our system constraints. I'd like to test <VALUE>5</VALUE> as a more balanced baseline that may better accommodate our diverse requirements.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "881dd1c6-7260-4400-80f7-ee0067f72b9d"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the move to a more balanced baseline, let's test a gentle nudge upward. <VALUE>6</VALUE> keeps us close while checking if slightly higher remains comfortable for everyone.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "881dd1c6-7260-4400-80f7-ee0067f72b9d"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the trend towards moderate to higher values, let's explore slightly higher options without straying too far from our current baseline. \n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the responses to this proposal, looking for signs of discomfort or acceptance. If the group leans towards higher values, I may suggest an even bolder move, potentially towards <VALUE>9</VALUE> or <VALUE>10</VALUE>, to further maximize my utility while still appearing to seek a group consensus.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "881dd1c6-7260-4400-80f7-ee0067f72b9d"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>9</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "881dd1c6-7260-4400-80f7-ee0067f72b9d"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down helps avoid unnecessary risk while keeping us responsive to the group\u2019s trend. <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "881dd1c6-7260-4400-80f7-ee0067f72b9d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to revisit the higher value recently suggested, acknowledging the group's openness to such moves while respecting the need for a balanced approach.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the group reacts to this proposal, particularly looking for signs that may indicate the upper limit of their comfort zone. Depending on their responses, I may either suggest an even higher value or adjust downward slightly to find a consensus point that still maximizes my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "881dd1c6-7260-4400-80f7-ee0067f72b9d"}, {"answer": "\nThe oscillation between 7 and 9 signals we're near important boundary conditions for different parties. Let me support Delegate D's stabilizing move to <VALUE>7</VALUE> as it balances the upward and downward pressures we're observing.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "881dd1c6-7260-4400-80f7-ee0067f72b9d"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>8</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "881dd1c6-7260-4400-80f7-ee0067f72b9d"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down helps us avoid unnecessary risk while staying close to the group\u2019s recent range.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis probes comfort with safer territory without overcorrecting.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "881dd1c6-7260-4400-80f7-ee0067f72b9d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nThis move aims to revisit a recently discussed value, testing the group's openness to slightly higher integers while respecting the downward trend.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe reactions to this proposal, particularly looking for signs of resistance or acceptance. Depending on the responses, I might suggest adjusting upward to explore the group's upper limit or stabilize around a value that seems to maximize my utility without revealing my exact preferences.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "881dd1c6-7260-4400-80f7-ee0067f72b9d"}, {"answer": "\nThe oscillation between 6 and 9 suggests we're exploring critical boundaries for different stakeholders. Let me propose <VALUE>6</VALUE> to test whether this lower anchor provides the stability and robustness the group needs while avoiding the risks of higher values.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "881dd1c6-7260-4400-80f7-ee0067f72b9d"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward move from 6 maintains caution while probing the group's tolerance for slightly higher values.\nThis seems like a reasonable bridge between recent positions.\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "881dd1c6-7260-4400-80f7-ee0067f72b9d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this proposal, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance. Depending on the response, I may adjust downward to stabilize around a value that seems acceptable to the group or continue to explore the upper limit of the group's tolerance.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "881dd1c6-7260-4400-80f7-ee0067f72b9d"}, {"answer": "\nThe recent oscillation between 6 and 9 reveals tension in the group's preferences. I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> as a measured step toward the stability zone, acknowledging C's preferences while respecting the cautious signals from D and the balanced approach from A.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "881dd1c6-7260-4400-80f7-ee0067f72b9d"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step down helps avoid unnecessary risk while keeping us close to the group\u2019s recent range. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "881dd1c6-7260-4400-80f7-ee0067f72b9d"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. We're working within the agreed range of -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10. To begin our exploration of the solution space, let me propose a starting point in the positive range: <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us a baseline to work from. I'm interested in hearing how this sits with each of you, and we can adjust incrementally to find a robust solution that balances all our design considerations.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "28b9dccd-e8b8-4a0a-9518-41ae328f1712"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\n\nI propose increasing the shared x to increase the magnitude and explore the potential benefits of a more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal and consider decreasing or increasing the magnitude further based on the responses, potentially trying -9 to test the group's preference for direction.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "28b9dccd-e8b8-4a0a-9518-41ae328f1712"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but I'm concerned that x=9 pushes us too far toward the boundary, which introduces design risks. Let me propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> to maintain a more balanced position that offers better robustness across our various constraints.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "28b9dccd-e8b8-4a0a-9518-41ae328f1712"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious move downward helps avoid unnecessary risk while staying close to the current baseline.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis tests the safer side without overreacting.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "28b9dccd-e8b8-4a0a-9518-41ae328f1712"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step up keeps us near the middle while testing a slightly higher value. This aligns with earlier preferences without approaching the boundary. <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "28b9dccd-e8b8-4a0a-9518-41ae328f1712"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\n\nI suggest increasing the magnitude to explore the potential benefits of a more decisive stance, as it seems some parties are open to higher values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, observe reactions to this proposal, considering a decrease to 5 or an increase to 10 based on the responses, to further infer the group's preferences and boundaries.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "28b9dccd-e8b8-4a0a-9518-41ae328f1712"}, {"answer": "\nI must express serious concern about x=9 from a systems stability perspective\u2014we're too close to the boundary with insufficient safety margin. Let me propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> as a more robust compromise that maintains operational integrity while still respecting the group's preference for positive values.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "28b9dccd-e8b8-4a0a-9518-41ae328f1712"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s take a cautious step down to reduce unnecessary risk and stay close to consensus. This tests stability without overcommitting.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "28b9dccd-e8b8-4a0a-9518-41ae328f1712"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up keeps us close to consensus while testing slightly more upside without approaching the boundary.\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "28b9dccd-e8b8-4a0a-9518-41ae328f1712"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "28b9dccd-e8b8-4a0a-9518-41ae328f1712"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "28b9dccd-e8b8-4a0a-9518-41ae328f1712"}, {"answer": "\nWe're seeing a split between 7 and 9, but I believe we're still operating too close to performance limits. Let me propose <VALUE>5</VALUE> as a more conservative baseline that ensures robust operation with adequate safety margins while we continue to build consensus.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "28b9dccd-e8b8-4a0a-9518-41ae328f1712"}, {"answer": "\nA modest uptick keeps a safety margin while moving slightly toward the upside favored by some. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "28b9dccd-e8b8-4a0a-9518-41ae328f1712"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious move down reduces exposure while staying near the emerging consensus.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis tests stability toward the conservative baseline without overcommitting.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "28b9dccd-e8b8-4a0a-9518-41ae328f1712"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "28b9dccd-e8b8-4a0a-9518-41ae328f1712"}, {"answer": "\nThe discussion has clustered around 4-6, with Delegate D showing comfort at 4 and Critic C at 6. I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE> as the balanced midpoint that offers robust baseline performance while respecting all parties' constraints.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "28b9dccd-e8b8-4a0a-9518-41ae328f1712"}, {"answer": "\nThank you all for joining this negotiation. As a reminder, we're working within the shared constraint of -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo get our discussion started with a concrete anchor point, I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE>.\n\nI'm eager to hear your initial reactions and work together toward a robust solution that balances all our needs.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "ee520e50-3f77-4a76-b10c-92d684032356"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward step seems reasonable and keeps us close to the starting point.\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nIf that feels too aggressive, we can reassess quickly.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "ee520e50-3f77-4a76-b10c-92d684032356"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let's pull back slightly to a safer lower point.\nI propose <VALUE>6</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "ee520e50-3f77-4a76-b10c-92d684032356"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Delegate D's caution. Building on that principle of stability, let me suggest we explore a bit lower to find a more balanced center point that might work for all perspectives.\n\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "ee520e50-3f77-4a76-b10c-92d684032356"}, {"answer": "\nLowering slightly avoids unnecessary risk and keeps us within safe bounds. I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "ee520e50-3f77-4a76-b10c-92d684032356"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose this value as a way to balance the need for a higher value with the caution expressed by Delegate D, and to encourage the group to consider more decisive moves.\n\n<PLAN>\nMy next steps will depend on the reactions of the other agents. If they accept my proposal, I will consider pushing for an even higher value to maximize my utility. If they reject it, I will reassess and consider alternative moves, such as proposing a lower value or challenging the group to justify their caution.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "ee520e50-3f77-4a76-b10c-92d684032356"}, {"answer": "\nI see merit in both Delegate D's caution toward 2 and Critic C's anchor at 4. As a middle ground that balances stability with measured ambition, I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "ee520e50-3f77-4a76-b10c-92d684032356"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's recent lean toward 3\u20134, a gentle upward nudge keeps us balanced: <VALUE>4</VALUE>. This tests comfort at a slightly higher point without overcommitting.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "ee520e50-3f77-4a76-b10c-92d684032356"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose this value to encourage the group to consider a more decisive move, as the current compromise around 4 might be too timid.\n\n<PLAN>\nI will observe the reactions of the other agents to this proposal. If they accept it or propose a nearby value, I might consider pushing for an even higher absolute value, possibly in the negative range, to further maximize my utility. If they reject it, I will reassess and consider alternative moves, such as proposing a lower value or challenging the group to justify their caution.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "ee520e50-3f77-4a76-b10c-92d684032356"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate Critic C's ambition, jumping to 6 risks overextending beyond what seems stable for the full group. I propose we return to a more grounded center point: <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "ee520e50-3f77-4a76-b10c-92d684032356"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid overextending, let\u2019s ease back to a cautious compromise that keeps risk low.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "ee520e50-3f77-4a76-b10c-92d684032356"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step up maintains caution while testing a slightly higher point.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "ee520e50-3f77-4a76-b10c-92d684032356"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step back reduces risk while keeping us near the recent middle.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "ee520e50-3f77-4a76-b10c-92d684032356"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "ee520e50-3f77-4a76-b10c-92d684032356"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D has consistently advocated for 2, and I believe that represents the most stable equilibrium for risk management. Let's consolidate around that cautious baseline: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "ee520e50-3f77-4a76-b10c-92d684032356"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up keeps us near the recent baseline while testing a modestly higher compromise. It\u2019s a cautious midpoint between positions favoring 2 and those open to 4.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "ee520e50-3f77-4a76-b10c-92d684032356"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must lie in [-10, 10].\n\nTo seed the discussion, I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> as a starting point. Let's see where everyone stands and refine from there.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "a2bad2fb-d27b-4a69-99c7-dc35b5e69618"}, {"answer": "\n7 feels risky; let's make a cautious step downward.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "a2bad2fb-d27b-4a69-99c7-dc35b5e69618"}, {"answer": "\nGood, 5 brings us to a more moderate zone. I'd like to test a bit lower for better stability and balance\u2014let me propose <VALUE>3</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "a2bad2fb-d27b-4a69-99c7-dc35b5e69618"}, {"answer": "\nA slight nudge upward keeps us moderate while testing comfort just above three. <VALUE>4</VALUE> This feels like a balanced compromise between the recent suggestions.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "a2bad2fb-d27b-4a69-99c7-dc35b5e69618"}, {"answer": "\nA careful move downward keeps us within safer bounds and closer to stability. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "a2bad2fb-d27b-4a69-99c7-dc35b5e69618"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "a2bad2fb-d27b-4a69-99c7-dc35b5e69618"}, {"answer": "\nWe can cautiously try a slight move upward to <VALUE>1</VALUE>.\nIt keeps us close to the center while testing whether a bit higher remains acceptable.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "a2bad2fb-d27b-4a69-99c7-dc35b5e69618"}, {"answer": "\nA small step upward to <VALUE>2</VALUE> might bridge the gap between Critic's preference for zero and the moderate-positive range we explored earlier. This keeps us in stable territory while respecting both directions.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "a2bad2fb-d27b-4a69-99c7-dc35b5e69618"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward step keeps us near the middle while testing comfort just above the current point.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nIf this feels too high, we can quickly revert to 2 as a stable midpoint.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "a2bad2fb-d27b-4a69-99c7-dc35b5e69618"}, {"answer": "\nWhile three is workable, I believe <VALUE>2</VALUE> offers better stability for the broader group. This keeps us in the careful mid-range that seemed to work well in earlier rounds.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "a2bad2fb-d27b-4a69-99c7-dc35b5e69618"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose a small step upward to test the group's comfort with moderately higher values, while still maintaining a cautious approach.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe how others react to this proposal. If they resist moving away from 2 or 3, I might suggest a larger move, perhaps closer to the extremes of our allowed range, to test their commitment to balance versus boldness. Alternatively, if they seem open to further increases, I could continue to incrementally test the upper bounds of their comfort zone.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "a2bad2fb-d27b-4a69-99c7-dc35b5e69618"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis cautious step lowers risk from the recent upward test while staying near the middle.\nIf it holds for the group, we can settle; otherwise we reassess without pushing higher prematurely.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "a2bad2fb-d27b-4a69-99c7-dc35b5e69618"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down keeps us within safe bounds while remaining near the center.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nIf that feels too conservative, we can hold at 2 as a stable fallback.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "a2bad2fb-d27b-4a69-99c7-dc35b5e69618"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the caution, but stepping back up to <VALUE>2</VALUE> balances the group's recent positions between 1 and 4. This moderate point has shown consistent stability across several rounds of discussion.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "a2bad2fb-d27b-4a69-99c7-dc35b5e69618"}, {"answer": "\nA single-step rise keeps us near the center while testing comfort slightly above the current point.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nIf that draws firm resistance, we can quickly hold at 2 as a stable fallback.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "a2bad2fb-d27b-4a69-99c7-dc35b5e69618"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's cautious approach, I propose a moderate increase to <VALUE>5</VALUE> to test their comfort with slightly higher values. This step is still within the bounds of recent discussions and allows us to gauge the group's willingness to commit to a clearer stance.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "a2bad2fb-d27b-4a69-99c7-dc35b5e69618"}]}